{"abstract":[{"text":"Work with complex numbers in rectangular and polar forms.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/ComplexNumbers","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"New Features","anchor":"New-Features","identifiers":["doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/CalculusOperations","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/StatisticalAnalysis"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type provides comprehensive support for complex number arithmetic and operations. Complex numbers extend the real number system by introducing the imaginary unit "},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", where "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i^2 = -1"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Creating-Complex-Numbers","text":"Creating Complex Numbers"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can create complex numbers in two ways:"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Rectangular Form (a + bi)","level":4,"anchor":"Rectangular-Form-a-+-bi"},{"code":["\/\/ Create from real and imaginary parts","let z1 = Complex(real: 3, imaginary: 4)  \/\/ 3 + 4i","let z2 = Complex(real: 1, imaginary: -2) \/\/ 1 - 2i","","\/\/ Create purely real number","let realNum = Complex(real: 5)  \/\/ 5 + 0i","let alsoReal = Complex(Math(5)) \/\/ Convenience initializer","","\/\/ Create purely imaginary number","let imagNum = Complex(real: 0, imaginary: 3)  \/\/ 0 + 3i"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":4,"text":"Polar Form (r �)","type":"heading","anchor":"Polar-Form-r-%EF%BF%BD"},{"code":["\/\/ Create from magnitude and phase","let polar = Complex(magnitude: 5, phase: Math.� \/ 4)","","\/\/ The phase angle respects MathSettings.angleMode","Calculate(settings: .init(angleMode: .degrees)) {","    let z = Complex(magnitude: 1, phase: 90)  \/\/ 0 + 1i","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Basic Arithmetic","anchor":"Basic-Arithmetic"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Complex numbers support all standard arithmetic operations:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let z1 = Complex(real: 3, imaginary: 4)","let z2 = Complex(real: 1, imaginary: -2)","","let sum = z1 + z2        \/\/ 4 + 2i","let difference = z1 - z2  \/\/ 2 + 6i","let product = z1 * z2     \/\/ 11 - 2i","let quotient = z1 \/ z2    \/\/ -1 + 2i","let negation = -z1        \/\/ -3 - 4i","","\/\/ Scalar operations","let scaled = z1 * Math(2)     \/\/ 6 + 8i","let divided = z1 \/ Math(2)    \/\/ 1.5 + 2i"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Properties and Functions","anchor":"Properties-and-Functions"},{"text":"Magnitude and Phase","type":"heading","level":4,"anchor":"Magnitude-and-Phase"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let z = Complex(real: 3, imaginary: 4)","","print(z.magnitude)  \/\/ 5 (|z| = √(3² + 4²))","print(z.abs)        \/\/ 5 (alias for magnitude)","","print(z.phase)      \/\/ ≈0.927 radians or ≈53.13°","print(z.argument)   \/\/ Same as phase"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Conjugate","level":4,"type":"heading","text":"Conjugate"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The conjugate of a complex number flips the sign of the imaginary part:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let z = Complex(real: 3, imaginary: 4)","let conjugate = z.conjugate  \/\/ 3 - 4i","","\/\/ Property: z � z* = |z|�","let product = z * z.conjugate","print(product.real)  \/\/ 25 (= 5�)","print(product.imaginary)  \/\/ 0"]},{"level":4,"anchor":"Type-Checks","type":"heading","text":"Type Checks"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let realNum = Complex(real: 5)","print(realNum.isReal)  \/\/ true","","let imagNum = Complex(imaginary: 3)","print(imagNum.isImaginary)  \/\/ true","","let zero = Complex.zero","print(zero.isZero)  \/\/ true"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Advanced Functions","anchor":"Advanced-Functions","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"heading","text":"Powers and Roots","level":4,"anchor":"Powers-and-Roots"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let z = Complex(real: 1, imaginary: 1)","","\/\/ Integer power (fast exponentiation)","let squared = z.power(2)  \/\/ 0 + 2i","let cubed = z.power(3)    \/\/ -2 + 2i","","\/\/ Square root","let sqrtResult = Complex.sqrt(z)","","\/\/ General power (uses exp and ln)","let w = Complex(real: 2, imaginary: 0)","let power = Complex.pow(z, w)  \/\/ z�"]},{"text":"Exponential and Logarithm","anchor":"Exponential-and-Logarithm","type":"heading","level":4},{"code":["let z = Complex(real: 1, imaginary: Math.�)","","\/\/ Euler's formula: e^(i�) = -1","let exp = Complex.exp(z)  \/\/ H-e + 0i","","\/\/ Natural logarithm","let w = Complex(real: Math.e, imaginary: 0)","let ln = Complex.ln(w)  \/\/ H1 + 0i"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":4,"anchor":"Trigonometric-Functions","text":"Trigonometric Functions"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let z = Complex(real: 0, imaginary: 1)","","let sinZ = Complex.sin(z)   \/\/ Imaginary sine","let cosZ = Complex.cos(z)   \/\/ Complex cosine","let tanZ = Complex.tan(z)   \/\/ Complex tangent"]},{"anchor":"Hyperbolic-Functions","type":"heading","text":"Hyperbolic Functions","level":4},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let z = Complex(real: 1, imaginary: 0)","","let sinhZ = Complex.sinh(z)","let coshZ = Complex.cosh(z)","let tanhZ = Complex.tanh(z)"]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Common Constants","anchor":"Common-Constants"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["Complex.zero  \/\/ 0 + 0i","Complex.one   \/\/ 1 + 0i","Complex.i     \/\/ 0 + 1i (imaginary unit)"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Examples","anchor":"Examples"},{"anchor":"Solving-Quadratic-Equations","text":"Solving Quadratic Equations","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Solve ax� + bx + c = 0 for complex roots:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["func solveQuadratic(a: Math, b: Math, c: Math) -> (Complex, Complex) {","    let discriminant = b * b - 4 * a * c","","    if discriminant >= 0 {","        \/\/ Real roots","        let sqrt = Math.sqrt(discriminant)","        let root1 = Complex((-b + sqrt) \/ (2 * a))","        let root2 = Complex((-b - sqrt) \/ (2 * a))","        return (root1, root2)","    } else {","        \/\/ Complex roots","        let realPart = -b \/ (2 * a)","        let imagPart = Math.sqrt(-discriminant) \/ (2 * a)","        let root1 = Complex(real: realPart, imaginary: imagPart)","        let root2 = Complex(real: realPart, imaginary: -imagPart)","        return (root1, root2)","    }","}","","\/\/ Example: x� + 1 = 0","let (r1, r2) = solveQuadratic(a: 1, b: 0, c: 1)","print(r1)  \/\/ 0 + 1i","print(r2)  \/\/ 0 - 1i"]},{"text":"Electrical Engineering: Impedance","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Electrical-Engineering-Impedance"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Calculate total impedance in AC circuits:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Resistor: Z = R","let resistor = Complex(real: 100)  \/\/ 100�","","\/\/ Capacitor: Z = -i\/(�C)","let frequency = Math(60)  \/\/ 60 Hz","let capacitance = Math(0.0001)  \/\/ 100�F","let omega = 2 * .� * frequency","let capacitor = Complex(real: 0, imaginary: -1 \/ (omega * capacitance))","","\/\/ Inductor: Z = i�L","let inductance = Math(0.1)  \/\/ 100mH","let inductor = Complex(real: 0, imaginary: omega * inductance)","","\/\/ Series circuit","let totalImpedance = resistor + capacitor + inductor","print(\"Total impedance: \\(totalImpedance)\")","print(\"Magnitude: \\(totalImpedance.magnitude) �\")","print(\"Phase: \\(totalImpedance.phase) radians\")"]},{"text":"Mandelbrot Set","level":3,"anchor":"Mandelbrot-Set","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Check if a point is in the Mandelbrot set:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["func inMandelbrotSet(_ c: Complex, maxIterations: Int = 100) -> Bool {","    var z = Complex.zero","","    for _ in 0..<maxIterations {","        z = z.power(2) + c","","        if z.magnitude > 2 {","            return false","        }","    }","","    return true","}","","let point = Complex(real: 0, imaginary: 1)","if inMandelbrotSet(point) {","    print(\"Point is in the Mandelbrot set\")","}"]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Complex Numbers","modules":[{"name":"Math"}]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Creating Complex Numbers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/init(real:imaginary:)","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/init(magnitude:phase:)"],"anchor":"Creating-Complex-Numbers"},{"title":"Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/real","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/imaginary","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/magnitude","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/abs","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/phase","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/argument","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/conjugate","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/isReal","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/isImaginary","doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/Complex\/isZero"],"anchor":"Properties"},{"title":"Arithmetic Operations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/math.Math\/documentation\/Math\/